The loan is for **5 months** at an annual simple‑interest rate of **10 %**.

1. **Compute the interest for the whole period**

\\\\\\\\[
\\\\\\\\text{Interest}=P \\\\\\\\times r \\\\\\\\times t
               = 3\\\\\\\\,650 \\\\\\\\times 0.10 \\\\\\\\times \\\\\\\\frac{5}{12}
               = 3\\\\\\\\,650 \\\\\\\\times 0.10 \\\\\\\\times 0.4167
               \\\\\\\\approx 152.08\\\\\\\\text{ dollars}
\\\\\\\\]

2. **Add the interest to the principal to get the total amount to be repaid**

\\\\\\\\[
\\\\\\\\text{Total amount}= 3\\\\\\\\,650 + 152.08 = 3\\\\\\\\,802.08\\\\\\\\text{ dollars}
\\\\\\\\]

3. **Divide by the number of monthly payments (5) to obtain the equal monthly instalment**

\\\\\\\\[
\\\\\\\\text{Monthly payment}= \\\\\\\\frac{3\\\\\\\\,802.08}{5}
                       \\\\\\\\approx 760.416\\\\\\\\text{ dollars}
\\\\\\\\]

\\\\\\\\[
\\\\\\\\boxed{\\\\\\\\text{Approximately } \\\\\\\\$760.42 \\\\\\\\text{ per month}}
